<div class="lead" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);">
  Project Broadsheet is a git clone away. The full source, 27 reader tools, nine editorial sections, RSS, search, SEO, and dark mode are already included and configured.
</div>

<section class="section-sm">
  <h2 class="h3">Prerequisites</h2>
  <ul style="list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-top: var(--space-sm); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; color: var(--text);">
    <li>Node.js 18 or later (<a href="https://nodejs.org">nodejs.org</a>)</li>
    <li>A GitHub account (free)</li>
    <li>A terminal. Any OS works, macOS, Linux, Windows.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<ol class="guide-steps">
  <li class="guide-step">
    <h2 class="guide-step__title">Clone the repo</h2>
    <div class="guide-step__body">
      <p>Pick whatever folder name fits your project.</p>
      <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/{{ meta.githubOwner }}/{{ meta.githubRepo }}.git my-publication
cd my-publication</code></pre>
    </div>
  </li>
  <li class="guide-step">
    <h2 class="guide-step__title">Install dependencies</h2>
    <div class="guide-step__body">
      <pre><code>npm install</code></pre>
      <p>Takes under a minute on a modern connection.</p>
    </div>
  </li>
  <li class="guide-step">
    <h2 class="guide-step__title">Run it locally</h2>
    <div class="guide-step__body">
      <pre><code>npm start</code></pre>
      <p>The site is now live at <code>http://localhost:8080</code> with hot reload. Open it in your browser, click through the sample pages, explore the reader tools.</p>
    </div>
  </li>
</ol>

<hr class="gold-rule">

<section class="section-sm">
  <h2 class="h3">Now what?</h2>
  <div class="grid grid-2" style="margin-top: var(--space-lg);">
    <a class="card card--link" href="/docs/getting-started/">
      <div class="card__eyebrow">Configure</div>
      <h3 class="card__title">Edit <code>site.json</code></h3>
      <p class="card__summary">Set your publication name, description, email, and which editorial sections you want.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="card card--link" href="/docs/design/">
      <div class="card__eyebrow">Brand</div>
      <h3 class="card__title">Edit <code>tokens.css</code></h3>
      <p class="card__summary">Change colors, typography, spacing, every design decision is a CSS variable.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="card card--link" href="/docs/content/">
      <div class="card__eyebrow">Write</div>
      <h3 class="card__title">Add your first article</h3>
      <p class="card__summary">Articles are Markdown files in <code>src/content/</code>. Create a file, add front matter, hit save.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="card card--link" href="/docs/deployment/">
      <div class="card__eyebrow">Deploy</div>
      <h3 class="card__title">Push to Cloudflare Pages</h3>
      <p class="card__summary">Connect your repo, set the build command, done. HTTPS and a custom domain are both free.</p>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

